.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH scanr-output-results 1  "scanr-output-results " 
.SH NAME
scanr\-output\-results \- Every probe result, with spans expanded; filter by host, port, or state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscanr\-output\-results\fR [\fB\-\-hosts\fR] [\fB\-\-ports\fR] [\fB\-\-states\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every probe result, with spans expanded; filter by host, port, or state
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-hosts\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Only these hosts: IPs, CIDR blocks, or ranges (repeatable, comma\-separated)
.TP
\fB\-\-ports\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Only these ports: `80`, `1\-1024`, or a list
.TP
\fB\-\-states\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Only these states: open, closed, filtered, error (comma\-separated)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: table]
Output shape: table, json, nmap, or list
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>

